---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="Read how Kreativ Auto uses affiliate links and what that means for recommendations." enableAds={false}>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface hero-frame p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">How affiliate links work here</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
            Some links on Kreativ Auto may be affiliate links. That means Kreativ Auto may earn a commission if a reader clicks through and makes a purchase.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-steel">
            That does not change the price a reader pays. It helps support the work when the recommendations are useful.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="accent-panel p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">Short version</p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
            <div class="soft-panel p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">Some links earn commission</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Kreativ Auto may earn from qualifying purchases, including through the Amazon Associates Program.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="soft-panel p-4">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">Reader price does not change</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The commission does not add a separate charge to the price paid by the reader.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">What this means in practice</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">How recommendations are handled</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Affiliate relationships do not guarantee inclusion</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The goal is still to point readers toward sensible options, not simply the most expensive product or the page with the most links.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Fitment matters more than the link</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Trim level, engine configuration, drivetrain, and exact part compatibility should always be checked before buying.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">A good recommendation still has limits</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">A product page can help narrow the shortlist, but it cannot replace proper diagnosis if the real problem has not been confirmed yet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Programs</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Current affiliate participation</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
        <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Kreativ Auto participates in the Amazon Associates Program.</li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Other affiliate relationships may exist where a product page or retailer link is genuinely useful to the reader.</li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">The presence of an affiliate link should not be read as a promise that the product is universally correct for every trim, market, or repair situation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Selection safeguards</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">How commercial links are kept in check</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Diagnosis comes first</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            A product guide should not push a part before the likely symptom area is clear. Several complaints can look similar until tires, brakes, battery health, leaks, or basic service history are checked.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Fitment remains the reader's final check</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            Retailer listings can change, and vehicle trim splits can be subtle. Readers should confirm exact year, engine, drivetrain, package, and market compatibility before ordering.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Not every useful item has a paid link</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            Some recommendations may point to manufacturer information, a category, or a diagnostic step instead of a retailer link when that is more useful than sending the reader to a cart.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Corrections are welcome</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
            If a product link changes, points to the wrong part, or misses an important compatibility warning, it can be flagged through the contact page for review.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
        Affiliate availability can change over time. If a retailer page changes, the product is no longer available, or the listing stops showing enough fitment detail, the guide may need to be updated or the link removed.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
